# `mdir check` warns when the force of a pair of charges jumps at the cutoff
# of PME by more than 1 kJ/mol/nm (D[pme-cutoff-jump-warning], #793): the
# jump is f |q_i q_j| [erfc(beta r_c)/r_c^2 + 2 beta exp(-beta^2 r_c^2)/(sqrt(pi) r_c)]
# for the largest |q_i q_j| of the pairs that the topology does not exclude.
# Mixed and double precision decide the pairs within a shell of some 1e-7 nm
# at the cutoff differently, and each changes the forces by up to the jump.
#
# The values are those of a NumPy reference in double precision on the
# prmtop of the solvated dipeptide in OPC (1183 charged particles in
# 19.8109 nm^3; f from CODATA 2022): the largest |q_i q_j|, of two virtual
# sites, is 1.84494 e^2; at the cutoff of 4.5 A with the beta of 9 A
# (0.347046 A^-1) erfc(beta r_c) = 2.7203e-2 and the jump is 229.065
# kJ/mol/nm, with 0.0318 pairs a frame in the shell of 3.54e-7 nm (the
# pull-in of the f32 cutoff of D159 and a unit in the last place of the
# largest edge in f32); at 9 A and tolerance = 1e-3 it is 4.0176 kJ/mol/nm.
# The tolerance of 1e-5, the default, gives 0.0678 at 9 A and 0.271 at 4.5 A,
# and no warning.
#
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
# RUN: cp %S/Inputs/opc/opc.prmtop %S/Inputs/opc/opc.inpcrd %t
# RUN: sed -n '/^#--- run.toml/,/^#--- end/p' %s | sed '1d;$d' > %t/default.toml
# RUN: sed -e 's|^cutoff = 9.0|cutoff = 4.5|' %t/default.toml > %t/short.toml
# RUN: sed -e 's|^\[pme\]|[pme]\nbeta = 0.3470459193712156|' %t/short.toml > %t/beta.toml
# RUN: sed -e 's|^\[pme\]|[pme]\ntolerance = 1e-3|' %t/default.toml > %t/loose.toml
#
# RUN: cd %t && mdir check beta.toml 2>&1 >/dev/null | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=BETA
# BETA: mdir: warning: PME with beta = 0.34705 Ang^-1 at the cutoff of 4.50 Ang has erfc(beta r_c) = 2.72E-02: the force of a pair of charges with |q_i q_j| = 1.8449 e^2 jumps by 229.06 kJ/mol/nm where it crosses the cutoff, more than 1 kJ/mol/nm. About 0.03 pairs of charged particles a frame lie within 3.5E-07 nm of the cutoff (from their mean density), where mixed precision may decide them differently from double, each changing the forces by up to the jump; the jump also degrades the conservation of energy in either precision. To derive beta from the cutoff, remove 'beta' of [pme], so that 'tolerance' (10^-5 by default) sets erfc(beta r_c)
#
# RUN: cd %t && mdir check --json beta.toml | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=JSON
# JSON: "code": "pme_cutoff_jump"
#
# RUN: cd %t && mdir check loose.toml 2>&1 >/dev/null | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=LOOSE
# LOOSE: at the cutoff of 9.00 Ang has erfc(beta r_c) = 1.00E-03: the force of a pair of charges with |q_i q_j| = 1.8449 e^2 jumps by 4.02 kJ/mol/nm
# LOOSE-SAME: To derive beta from the cutoff, set 'tolerance' of [pme] to 10^-5 (the default) or less
#
# The defaults: no warning, at 9 A and at 4.5 A.
# RUN: cd %t && mdir check default.toml 2>&1 >/dev/null | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=NONE --allow-empty
# RUN: cd %t && mdir check short.toml 2>&1 >/dev/null | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=NONE --allow-empty
# NONE-NOT: pme_cutoff_jump
# NONE-NOT: jumps by
#
# The run itself is unchanged: `mdir run` does not print it.
# RUN: cd %t && mdir run beta.toml 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=LOG
# LOG: Coulomb reciprocal
# LOG-NOT: jumps by

#--- run.toml
[input]
topology    = "opc.prmtop"
coordinates = "opc.inpcrd"
[output]
energy_interval = 0
[energy]
cutoff = 9.0
electrostatics = "PME"
[pme]
[dynamics]
integrator = "VELOCITY_VERLET"
time_step  = 0.001
steps      = 0
[ensemble]
ensemble    = "NVE"
temperature = 0.0
[constraints]
rigid_water = true
[boundary]
type = "PERIODIC"
#--- end
